  body=sub(t['name'],t['note'],'Terpene profile')+f'<section class="section"><div class="wrap article-layout"><article class="article"><h2>Get to know the aroma</h2><p>{t["text"]}</p><div class="callout"><p class="eyebrow">Read the actual panel</p><p>{t["tip"]}</p></div><h2>Use this in a San Jose dispensary</h2><p>Ask whether the product you are considering has a terpene report for its current batch. Confirm the compound name and units before comparing it with another package. If the report is unavailable, treat the terpene composition as unknown rather than borrowing numbers from a similarly named cultivar.</p><h2>What the reference tells you</h2><p>The molecular formula and molecular weight identify a chemical reference record. They are not a product potency rating, a recommended dose, or a promise of an effect. The aroma labels are editorial descriptions used to make the directory easier to explore.</p><h2>Follow the source</h2><p>{a(t["source"],"Open PubChem compound record ↗")}. Chemical data checked {prop.get("checked_at",DATE)[:10]}. Descriptive content reviewed {E["editorial_reviewed"]}.</p><p>{a("index.html","Explore all terpene profiles ↗")}</p></article>{side}</div></section>'+guides_section()
